From 8822c2f54dd64b3848d8a397634c8a34782ce1b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:14:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 569/572] fix(psci): ignore pending FIQs during CPU_SUSPEND

Check only the IRQ bit in ISR_EL1 when deciding whether a pending
interrupt should abort CPU_SUSPEND. The non-secure caller must disable
IRQ interrupts that should not wake the CPU before requesting suspend.

Moreover, this check runs before the SPD suspend callback,
so before its management of secure interrupts; a pending FIQ here does
not necessarily indicate a wake-up interrupt.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 2b8feb9eee64107070cb0143931ae659b7b55d0e fix(psci): ignore pending FIQs during CPU_SUSPEND]
Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Ic1ba3841fdddaba1dc52c3ff2fa7b65f9c8fa4d7
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/625301
Reviewed-by: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 lib/psci/psci_suspend.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/psci/psci_suspend.c b/lib/psci/psci_suspend.c
index ca46762d9e..ee9dd2e637 100644
--- a/lib/psci/psci_suspend.c
+++ b/lib/psci/psci_suspend.c
@@ -138,11 +138,11 @@ int psci_cpu_suspend_start(unsigned int idx,
 	psci_acquire_pwr_domain_locks(end_pwrlvl, parent_nodes);
 
 	/*
-	 * We check if there are any pending interrupts after the delay
+	 * We check if there are any pending NS interrupts (IRQ) after the delay
 	 * introduced by lock contention to increase the chances of early
 	 * detection that a wake-up interrupt has fired.
 	 */
-	if (read_isr_el1() != 0U) {
+	if ((read_isr_el1() & BIT(ISR_I_SHIFT)) != 0U) {
 		goto suspend_exit;
 	}
 
